!scope=row|1940–41 
| rowspan=6 colspan=15|''No competitive football was played between 1939 and 1946 due to the [[World War II|Second World War]]. Celtic entered unofficial competitions including the [[1939–40 Scottish Emergency League|1939–40 Emergency League]], the [[Scottish War Emergency Cup|1940 Emergency Cup]], the [[Southern Football League (Scotland)|Southern League]], the [[Summer Cup (Scottish football)|Summer Cup]], the [[Southern League Cup (Scotland)|Southern League Cup]] and the [[1946 Victory Cup]].''
